{
  "_note": "Song forms (docs/song-engine-v2-prd.md R7) and the song-length plan (docs/song-builder-prd.md B2–B3). A form is the song's running order, as section ids from data/song-section-templates.json. A section that plays more than once reuses its material; `variation` names a controlled change from `variations` (the only difference verify allows between repeats). Each slot plays its section's material `times` times in a row, between `min` and `max`. lib/songLength.ts picks the form and every slot's `times` for a target length at the feel's tempo: it grows each form from its minimum one step at a time, in `growth` order (a step adds one more time to every slot with that `grow` tag that can still grow), keeps the step closest to the target, then nudges single slots tagged `fine` up or down one time at a time while that brings it closer (so the plan isn't stuck on the coarse steps). Among forms that land within `toleranceBars`, it keeps the cheapest by `formCost` + `stepCost` × steps + the miss in bars (so a longer song gets a fuller form before it gets more repeats); if none lands that close, the closest. Standard is the form at the default length (3:15).",
